          "html": "The 2023 Finals had little to do with the altitude in Denver when the series began. Simply put, the Nuggets <a href=\"https://www.nba.com/news/5-takeaways-nuggets-win-title-game-5\">were just that much better</a>."
        },
        {
          "index": 22,
          "text": "Jamal Murray, who suffered an ACL injury in April 2021, played in his first postseason since the 2020 games held in Orlando during the COVID-19 pandemic. Murray averaged 21.4 points, 10 assists and 6.4 rebounds against Miami. Caldwell-Pope, Michael Porter Jr., Aaron Gordon, Bruce Brown and rookie Christian Braun played key minutes in the series, too.",
          "links": [],
