          "links": [],
          "html": "<span style=\"font-size: 1.125rem\">As strong as the Lakers were, though, the rest of the West proved formidable. The Hornets took flight with a 56-26 season sparked by their All-Star duo of David West and Chris Paul. In San Antonio, the Spurs finished 56-26 as well and rode Tim Duncan, Tony Parker and Manu Ginobili to great success. The Phoenix Suns, Houston Rockets and Utah Jazz rounded out the West’s top six teams, with 50-win teams in Dallas and Denver rounding things out.</span>"
