          "index": 11,
          "text": "Before 2007-08 got started, many wondered whether Pierce, Garnett and Allen could coexist in Boston. That was quickly put to rest, though, as Boston got off to an 18-2 start and finished an NBA-best 66-16 — the Celtics’ best regular-season mark since going 67-15 in 1985-86. In addition, the Celtics pulled off the best single-season turnaround in league history, improving by 24 wins from their 2006-07 finish.",
          "links": [],
          "html": "Before 2007-08 got started, many <span style=\"font-size: 1.125rem\">wondered whether Pierce, Garnett and Allen could coexist in Boston. That was quickly put to rest, though, as Boston got off to an 18-2 start and finished an NBA-best 66-16 — the Celtics’ best regular-season mark since going 67-15 in 1985-86. In addition, the Celtics pulled off the best single-season turnaround in league history, improving by 24 wins from their 2006-07 finish.&nbsp;</span>"
