          "html": "In the West, the infusion of Gasol to the Lakers’ lineup had L.A. looking fierce for the playoffs. The first round featured the Hornets ousting the West’s defending champions, the Mavs, in five games. Phoenix’s trade for O’Neal went bust in the playoffs as he wasn’t much of a factor against the rival Spurs in a five-game series loss. The Lakers did not disappoint overall, sweeping the Nuggets in the first round and outlasting the Jazz in the West semifinals before dropping the Spurs in Game 5 to reach The Finals."
